    "description": "What: the END-TO-END minefield chain (Minefields MR-19, CE-2443 / CE-4624): a Friend 'Patrol' (Man Leader + Man 1-3, under 'HQ' running SupportCommand) marches east along y 80 to (135, 80) — INSIDE 'Field D' (KG-7: no way round, the order goes through; a march to a point past the field simply goes round it, measured), an enemy anti-personnel field it does not know (x 120-140, y 65-95, a mine every 3 m). A mine goes off; the patrol halts (MineStrike) and asks for engineers; the HQ sends its 'Engineers' (a TKB 116 'Clearer', 'Sapper 3', the 'Sapper Team' of 'Sapper 1-2'): a man traces and MARKS the field (ReconMinefield), then the clearer cuts a LANE along the patrol's line (Breach / ClearLane); the patrol crosses THROUGH the lane and reaches its objective. Judge: a strike; the mark; the lane cleared and known to Friend; every patrol man inside the lane while in the field; the objective reached; no second strike. ⏳ RED at S3 (2026-11-19): the patrol is under the HQ and a commanded squad never reacts MinefieldAhead (CE-5040, behaviors); S1/S2/S9 pass, S11 breaks at 174 s (the second mine). The inside-the-lane rows are added once the chain runs past S3. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh mf-clear-lane-and-cross"
